// Where a dropped block would land, in the picture's own coordinates. A reporter
// goes into the pill under the point; a statement goes into a stack, before or
// after the row under the point by which half of it the point is in: the upper
// half puts it before the row, the lower half after it (inside the body when the row
// opens one, as the last line of the if when the row is its else, and after a
// whole C-block when the point is on its cap). A hat is not a place to put a
// block before; the first line of its body is. The answer is the kind of drop
// (conf.id's bkk_d_), then the line to insert at and its indent, or the box.

